From 0498312fc6aafc0c52ad270e9245245fd1756f7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:41:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Memory types: documentation, stricter test

- The documentation tells that an application creating its own
  mfem::Device keeps the memory types of MFEM, unless it calls
  mfem::Device::SetMemoryTypes before, and that MFEM_MEMORY=host gives
  the memory of the device allocated by the runtime of the GPU, without
  pool.
- DeviceOptionTest checks the memory of the device without GPU (the one
  of the host) and prints the expected memory types on failure.
- The comment of setMemoryTypes no longer mentions MFEM_DEVICE, with
  which initialize fails before.
---
 docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst |  9 ++++++---
 docs/source/user_guide/tutorial.rst           |  4 +++-
 include/MFEMMGIS/Config.hxx                   |  4 +++-
 src/Config.cxx                                |  2 +-
 tests/CMakeLists.txt                          |  3 ++-
 tests/DeviceOptionTest.cxx                    | 20 ++++++++++++++-----
 6 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
